{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/692199-extempore-pandorans","id":692199,"title":"Extempore Pandorans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-07T03:32:54-07:00","id":692199,"title":"Extempore Pandorans?","content":"As I'm sure we all know, sometimes circumstances allow for a promethean to arise spontaneously.<br /> <br /> Well, do you think those circumstances can get it wrong enough to create pandorans instead? <br /> <br /> Storywise, I don't think it makes much of a difference.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it could justify some really odd pandorans, since they tend to be reflections of prometheans, so a pandoran that reflects a hypothetical unique promethean could have some surprising features.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm not sure how restrained Promethean STs are when it comes to getting creative with pandorans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:27:03-07:00","id":693997,"title":"","content":"I don't see why it couldn't happen, unless you decide that Pandorans arise from the personal flaws of the prospective maker (be they human or Promethean) messing up the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T15:09:59-07:00","id":695401,"title":"","content":"well, if a potential Demiurge can accidentally make a Pandoran instead of a Promethean (like in Seattle), I don't think that it is out of the question for a Pandoran to rise spontaneously like a Promethean- like maybe in cases Flux goes wild and rip dead bodies apart into some form of &quot;zombie invasion&quot; :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:37:14-07:00","id":695609,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. The more interesting question is how the Pandoran in question reflects what went wrong in the circumstance. For example, you could even alter the rules for Dormancy to create a Cthulhu-like Pandoran that rises and slumbers not when seen by mortals, but according to some cosmological cycle that was put into motion by a botched ritual or scientific experiment. Or maybe it was already &quot;alive&quot;, and the calamity broke a finely tuned series of barriers between here and Somewhere Else, allowing an unfathomable entity to send a tiny fraction of themselves to Earth. This fraction looks and behaves somewhat like a Pandoran, but not everything fits. Is the Flux present in other realities, or is it simply piggybacking on an unrelated disaster?<br /> <br /> I felt pretty inspired by this idea, so have some plot hooks.<br /> <br /> One of these supposed Extempore Pandorans looks almost like a Promethean, with minor Disfigurements and almost-but-not-really-human mannerisms. It has gotten into its head that it is the first of its kind that can achieve a New Dawn, and it is learning about humans and Prometheans very fast. It might know secrets and lore about famous Prometheans and their Pilgrimages. However, its presence seems to make normal Pandorans curiously humble. Some follow it around and bring it gutted and rotting gifts like a cat would. Others kneel beside it and recite chants in guttural voices in a manner suggestive of worship. Is there something more to this? Can this Pandoran actually become human, or is he a charlatan using some obscure Transmutation? It does not become Dormant like other Pandorans as far as most can tell, and this immunity is apparently transferred to its followers. The members of this cult of sorts are fiercely protective and obedient, but even then, it doesn't really control them, and getting past their snapping jaws is another risk. If the PCs get an audience with it, what might be asked in return for its knowledge? What if this quest comes to a bad end, and the New Dawn turns out to be a New Dusk, a harrowing process that results in something beyond the confines of Flux-tainted flesh?<br /> <br /> (As a side note, I can easily see <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-682\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-682</b></a> from the SCP Foundation as an Extempore Pandoran. In its Experiment Log, as well as the Foundation Tales and fanart where it appears, its intellect and cunning are on par with that of a Sublimatus, and its powers reek of Pandoran Transmutations. It becomes Dormant when submerged in hydrochloric acid, but being awake and around humans is no more pleasant in its eyes. It appears to be capable of regaining Pyros without eating the flesh of Prometheans. Perhaps the circumstance behind its &quot;birth&quot; influenced its visceral hatred of all life in our universe? If someone took the Flux out of it, what would be left? Could a Centimanus study its carcass and develop a Transmutation similar to its dynamic evolution?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-08-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:01:49-07:00","id":714126,"title":"","content":"Totally could. Just as an FYI, we removed the &quot;Pandorans have splats that map to Promethean Lineages&quot; in 2nd Ed, mostly because I've never seen it as necessary (and we didn't have space to do it justice anyway). <b>Pandora's Book</b> gets into Flux-tainted areas and things like Pandorans that can happen &quot;naturally,&quot; so the precedent is there. If we get a <b>Night Horrors</b> book for <b>Promethean</b>, that's totally a concept I'd use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:59:22-07:00","id":718870,"title":"","content":"New hints toward Promethean is always nice- and more freeform Pandorans sounds exciting. The idea of the mirrored splats was really great for Storytelling, but I feel like making your own unique horrors will turn out nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:11:17-08:00","id":769910,"title":"","content":"While I vehemently disagree with removing the Mockeries for the Lineages, due to finding the official reasoning not acceptable when it comes to the themes of Promethean and my knowledge of in game and irl alchemy and mundane science ( regardless of whether or not you mix bleach and vinegar together intentionally , for example, the reaction will still be chlorine gas- just replace bleach and vinegar with Flux and a failed Lineage intended generation of a Promethean and the chlorine as the resulting Pandoran), the idea proposed is very fascinating.<br /> <br /> I won't lie, I would of preferred it if Mockeries existed along side the unique Pandorans, like with recent events involving Beast and Mage I am both saddened and incredibly disappointed with the misappropriation of potential, but I'll get over it XD<br /> <br /> Whew, gripping over! 682 as an Pandoran would be terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-20-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T18:01:19-08:00","id":770417,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm a little disappointed myself, I imagine most promethean STs feel free to make their own pandorans if they feel so inclined anyway, but oh well, not the end of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}